[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"372","stub":{"id":"372","section":"10. Below Filter Plant to Picnic Rock Access","altname":"Filter Plant","river":"Cache La Poudre","difficulty":"IItoIII","states":["USA-COL"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"low-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"373","dateTime":"2026-05-11T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"portage","description":"The Gateway Diversion Dam is located upstream of Gateway Park and means that it's not possible to link Filter Plant with the sections upstream. The dam serves to divert water for municipal use for the City of Fort Collins. American Whitewater is working to address public safety at this high hazard low-head dam and provide for boat and fish passage.","id":"WgRg5UVJv3a5MGs8Oegf3","location":{"latitude":"40.701068","longitude":"-105.247696"},"name":"Low-head dam above put-in","distance":"-0.8","photoID":"EvZ926O5QFldcr8uf7PSF","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"put-in","description":"The most convenient put-in for Filter Plant, Gateway Natural Area &lt;<https://www.fcgov.com/naturalareas/finder/gateway>&gt; is owned by the City of Fort Collins. It has a large parking lot, picnic areas, and a boat ramp. Entry costs $8/day, or an annual pass is $40/year. Gateway Natural Area seems to be the only place that the City charges for entry, but the annual pass is separate from County and State annual passes.","id":"107735","location":{"latitude":"40.699603","longitude":"-105.245527"},"name":"Gateway Natural Area put-in","distance":"0.13","photoID":"1LTz6jjfd3LoQwNhSXXl0","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"put-in","description":"A short distance downstream of Gateway Natural Area, the US Forest Service maintains a set of wooden stairs to access the river. Limited free roadside parking is available here, but watch for traffic. Google Maps link: <https://goo.gl/maps/2MAr214Vk6PvuzJGA>","id":"gt736wcYIqs6NSmntW0s7","location":{"latitude":"40.694538","longitude":"-105.242182"},"name":"Forest Service put-in","distance":"0.64","photoID":"10cxvhIiNuDtmfNM2li7W","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"The river makes a sharp left-hand turn, with a wave train here. The waves can be substantial at high water.","id":"DYs0cQTTixRCMO3FS85fr","location":{"latitude":"40.690484","longitude":"-105.239024"},"name":"Screaming Left-Hand Turn","distance":"0.97","difficulty":"II","approximate":false,"photoID":"JeqPugC2S2BLhh0tilZ9S"},{"type":"rapid","description":"This rapid is shortly above the road bridge, where the river splits around an island. The left channel is wider and deeper, and the right channel closes off at flows below about 800 cfs. The two channels rejoin below the island, creating swirly eddy lines that have caused more than one beginner kayaker to swim.","id":"9Nzs3x9iOkzXf3hQPJNAH","location":{"latitude":"40.686457","longitude":"-105.238392"},"name":"Sluicebox Rapid","distance":"1.52","difficulty":"II","approximate":false,"photoID":"f8ffTrRiZMm2ESbocH5F5"},{"type":"rapid","description":"This rapid is on a sharp right turn shortly below the road bridge. It has a large rock or hole in the middle, with cobbles stretching from the center rock to the left shore. Tailwaves then stretch a short distance downstream. At low water, the rock is passable in a narrow channel along the right shore. At flows above about 1200 cfs, a wider left line is also available. It's possible to road-scout Mad Dog from a couple of pull-outs, and possible to scout from river level by landing on a small beach around the corner upstream. The river scout doesn't have much of a trail; you're more likely to get injured by stepping on a cactus while scouting than by running the rapid blind. This rapid is named for Brian \"Mad Dog\" Maddox, a longtime Poudre Canyon resident, kayaker extraordinaire, and author of \"River Guide to the Cache La Poudre River.\"","id":"kH0CdUGPImUAwnupYhqh8","location":{"latitude":"40.68443","longitude":"-105.237638"},"name":"Mad Dog Rapid","distance":"1.85","difficulty":"II+","approximate":false,"photoID":"1ITP9exND904uJqzCK1xk"},{"type":"other","description":"The straightaway below Mad Dog begins the easier water of the second half of the run","id":"zwY73Mk4PK6nz57v3pEVK","location":{"latitude":"40.68199","longitude":"-105.236722"},"name":"Margarita Flats","distance":"2.08","photoID":null,"difficulty":"I+","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"The last rapid just upstream of the take-out.","id":"fW9CRxLn8PNk8Cep4NCUG","location":{"latitude":"40.67117897","longitude":"-105.23692676"},"name":"360 Rapid","distance":"2.91","difficulty":"II-","approximate":false,"photoID":"pkk2w2B35atG2SoZkHT4f"},{"type":"takeout","description":"Picnic Rock takeout offers free parking, picnic shelters, a bathroom, and a few places to take a boat out of the river. It's not possible to drive quite to the river's edge anywhere, so a short boat carry is required.","id":"112974","location":{"latitude":"40.670192","longitude":"-105.231194"},"name":"Picnic Rock takeout","distance":"3.22","photoID":"Erir67p0HyrTt3OYpK9eK","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"hazard","description":"A short distance below the takeout is a low-head dam. Don't try to keep boating!","id":"8ZvLn0cLfCpGA7oKciCow","location":{"latitude":"40.670626","longitude":"-105.227854"},"name":"Low head dam below takeout","distance":"3.45","photoID":"vo3M0aFkepwALsWCxnXcW","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"Erir67p0HyrTt3OYpK9eK","ext":"jpg","post_id":"9dFSpd4XheeTfOmYhnohG","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe","poi_id":"112974","photo_date":"2025-05-31T21:34:11.000Z","updated_at":"2025-06-02T21:34:17.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/Erir67p0HyrTt3OYpK9eK","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/Erir67p0HyrTt3